1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,629
Welcome to Melody and
Barnaby's Music Nuggets!

2
00:00:05,529 --> 00:00:09,939
Have you ever looked at music and wondered
what all those lines and dots actually mean?

3
00:00:09,989 --> 00:00:11,820
Let's find out!

4
00:00:12,420 --> 00:00:16,389
Today we are going to
learn some musical names.

5
00:00:16,989 --> 00:00:19,982
Music is written on
five lines like this.

6
00:00:20,082 --> 00:00:21,683
Count them with me!

7
00:00:21,733 --> 00:00:22,633
One.

8
00:00:22,683 --> 00:00:23,676
Two.

9
00:00:23,726 --> 00:00:24,812
Three.

10
00:00:24,862 --> 00:00:25,808
Four.

11
00:00:25,858 --> 00:00:27,005
Five.

12
00:00:27,055 --> 00:00:30,002
Five lines together
are called a stave.

13
00:00:31,302 --> 00:00:34,752
This swirly symbol next
to me is called a clef.

14
00:00:34,802 --> 00:00:37,500
It tells us how high or low to play.

15
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:42,405
This one is called the treble clef,
and it is used for higher sounds!

16
00:00:43,005 --> 00:00:46,145
And this clef looks totally different.

17
00:00:46,195 --> 00:00:49,035
Two dots and a curl.

18
00:00:49,085 --> 00:00:52,871
That's the bass clef,
for lower sounds!

19
00:00:53,471 --> 00:00:56,091
This little blob with a
stick is called a note.

20
00:00:56,141 --> 00:01:00,041
It sits on the stave to
show us which sound to play.

21
00:01:00,741 --> 00:01:03,688
A note can sit on a
line, like this one,

22
00:01:03,738 --> 00:01:07,381
or in the gap between two
lines, which we call a space.

23
00:01:08,681 --> 00:01:14,136
Sometimes a note is too high
or too low to fit on the stave.

24
00:01:14,336 --> 00:01:19,095
We give it a tiny extra line
to stand on. A ledger line.

25
00:01:20,495 --> 00:01:22,556
Let's say them one more time:

26
00:01:22,606 --> 00:01:23,692
Stave.

27
00:01:23,742 --> 00:01:24,828
Clef.

28
00:01:24,878 --> 00:01:25,871
Note.

29
00:01:25,921 --> 00:01:27,750
Line and space.

30
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:29,071
Ledger line.

31
00:01:29,121 --> 00:01:30,321
Brilliant!

32
00:01:31,304 --> 00:01:32,765
Now it's your turn!

33
00:01:32,865 --> 00:01:37,065
Open Name That Part, and
show what you've learned!

34
00:01:37,165 --> 00:01:39,555
See you for the next Nugget!

